  "question": {
    "text": "As shown below, bob \\(A\\) of a pendulum having massless string of length ' \\(R\\) ' is released from \\(60^{\\circ}\\) to the vertical. It hits another bob \\(B\\) of half the mass that is at rest on a friction less table in the center. Assuming elastic collision, the magnitude of the velocity of bob A after the collision will be (take g as acceleration due to gravity.)\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/qwxgUN5rQ-iLDMPg0MmpL6T-1Z0UpQQQmtsJY3r3IeU.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "v5V89",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{4}{3} \\sqrt{\\operatorname{Rg}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "k0Dnf",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{2}{3} \\sqrt{\\mathrm{Rg}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CTYpS",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{\\mathrm{Rg}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hN9Rl",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{3} \\sqrt{\\operatorname{Rg}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/m2cxs0mBoIhp4yd5_SLNfGZ_ypwnxZrkk0eA9gzcm7w.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\nVelocity of a just before hitting :\n$\\mathrm{u}=\\sqrt{2 \\mathrm{~g} \\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{2}}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{gR}}$\n\nJust after collision, let velocity of A and B are $\\mathrm{v}_1$ and $v_2$ respectively\n$\\therefore \\text { by COM: }$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& m u=m v_1+\\frac{m}{2} v_2 \\\\\n& 2 v_1+v_2=2 u ...(i)\\\\\n& e=1=\\frac{v_2-v_1}{u} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow v_2-v_1=u..(ii)\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nFrom (i) -(ii)\n$\\Rightarrow 3 \\mathrm{v}_1=\\mathrm{u} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{v}_1=\\frac{\\mathrm{u}}{3}=\\frac{1}{3} \\sqrt{\\mathrm{gR}}$",
    "image": null
  },
